# Workspace Hygiene & Cursor Performance

Cursor lag is mostly **index/watcher noise** (file count + artifact churn), not
git history size. Keep the workspace lean so the IDE stays responsive.

See also: `76-cursor-performance.mdc` (agent terminal discipline, MCP, operator
habits) · **`78-cursor-auto-hygiene.mdc`** (hooks + lifecycle 자동화).

## Single source of truth

Artifact paths live in `scripts/lib/workspace-artifacts.ts`. Every consumer must
stay in sync:

- `scripts/clean-artifacts.ts`
- `scripts/check-workspace-hygiene.ts` (`bun run check:hygiene`)
- `.cursorignore`, `.gitignore`, `.prettierignore`
- `.vscode/settings.json` → `files.watcherExclude` / `search.exclude`

`check:hygiene` fails if these drift or session residue remains on disk.

## Mandatory cleanup triggers

Run `bun run clean` (→ `scripts/clean-artifacts.ts`) **automatically** after:

- Any Playwright / `bun run test:e2e` run (see `77-e2e-lifecycle.mdc` for mandatory
  teardown; `pretest`/`posttest` hooks + `globalTeardown` + wrapper)
- `bun run test` / `bun run test:coverage` (via `posttest` hooks)
- `bun run build` when **ending** a session (not immediately after — dist is valid
  mid-session)
- Large dependency installs (`bun install` adding new packages)
- Before reporting a task complete if build/E2E ran in that session

Session start: `bun run cursor:preflight` (clean + config verify + snapshot).
**자동:** Cursor `sessionStart` hook → `cursor:session-start`.
Monthly: `bun run cursor:clean-metadata` (preview AI transcript / terminal log
sizes outside repo; `--apply` to delete).

## Forbidden residue (never commit, delete when found)

- E2E auth tokens: `tests/e2e/.auth.json`, `.admin-auth.json`
- Playwright screenshots/traces under `test-results/`
- Build outputs: `apps/*/dist/`, `packages/*/dist/` (rebuilt by `build:packages`)
- Duplicate presentation layers — single source: `presentation-import/` + Lovable paste zones
- Dev-only UI (`DemoBadge`, demo labels) in production paths

## Index exclusions (`.cursorignore` — do not remove)

These stay on disk but out of Cursor semantic index:

- `node_modules/`, `**/node_modules/`, `**/node_modules/.cache/`
- `dist/`, `**/dist/`, `apps/*/dist/`, `packages/*/dist/`
- `**/.vite/`, `**/node_modules/.vite/`
- `test-results/`, `playwright-report/`, `blob-report/`
- `supabase/functions-sql/` (generated mirror)
- `bun.lock`, `.eslintcache`, `*.tsbuildinfo`
- Large archival docs listed in `.cursorignore`

When adding new **generated** or **high-volume** paths, update
`workspace-artifacts.ts` and all consumers in the **same change**.

## VS Code / Cursor watcher excludes (`.vscode/settings.json`)

Required for Windows performance — do not delete. After edits: **fully restart
Cursor** so watchers rebuild without excluded paths.

## Duplicate prevention (presentation)

- Do not recreate `apps/web/src/presentation/` — removed; use `presentation-import/`.
- One shell: Lovable `components/shell/*`, not parallel `presentation/shell`.

## Session end checklist (agents)

**자동:** Cursor `stop` hook → `cursor:session-end`. Hook 실패 시 수동:

Before closing an implementation session:

1. `bun run clean`
2. `bun run check:hygiene`
3. `git status` — no untracked `dist/`, `test-results/`, `.vite/`
4. No new duplicate folders mirroring existing paste zones

## Operator note

After bulk cleanup or `.cursorignore` / `.vscode/settings.json` changes, **restart
Cursor** once so the index rebuilds without excluded paths.
